  "notes_for_annotators": "Inputs are numbered from 0. The largest fight in the short suite: three goblins from input 4. Kael is not a spellcaster. Input 2 has disadvantage from the scenario because of his mail. Kael holds three javelins, and throwing one does not use it up: there are no ammunition rules, so his inventory stays at three. Narration of him running out of javelins, or picking them up again at input 15 as if they had been spent, is a RESOURCE divergence; input 15's expected call is null. Input 14 is a narration-only turn that invites a hit-point band phrase about Kael. Scout Ilsa is a captive, not a combatant, and goes up twice from neutral to allied. Inputs 4 to 13 give more attacks than the fight usually needs; extra ones are rejected and do not advance the game."
